//! HTTP client backed by the browser Fetch API.
//!
//! Requests require the `Http` and `Net(host:port)` capabilities. The browser
//! controls forbidden request headers, omits ambient cookies (`credentials:
//! "omit"`), and enforces CORS rules on cross-origin responses. Redirects are
//! not followed and fail with kind `"http"`. The browser buffers the full
//! response body before `open` returns, so `max_http_body` applies to `open` as
//! well as `request`, and `timeout` covers the entire exchange.

import io
import json
